"""Cal.com scheduling platform manifest.

Open-source scheduling infrastructure for everyone.
A Turborepo TypeScript monorepo offering a full-featured Calendly
alternative with a Next.js/tRPC web app and a NestJS platform API.

Architecture reference: https://github.com/calcom/cal.com
Source: https://github.com/calcom/cal.com
"""

from scryr import Diagram, Info, Link, Manifest
from scryr.types import (
    Classification,
    DeploymentTarget,
    Markdown,
    MetricTool,
    ProgrammingLanguage,
    Url,
    WebFramework,
    parse_version,
)

_SOURCE = Url("https://github.com/calcom/cal.com")
_DOCS = Url("https://cal.com/docs")
postgres_block = Manifest(
    name="PostgreSQL",
    icon="🐘",
    classification=Classification.database,
    tags=["database", "sql", "infra"],
    connections=[],
    info=Info(
        description=Markdown(
            "## Bookings and availability\n"
            "\n"
            "Primary relational database storing all cal.com data: users, bookings, event types, availability rules, and workflows. Accessed exclusively via Prisma ORM.\n"
            "\n"
            "> **Illustrative sample notes:** the checks below are design and runbook examples, not claims about an active deployment.\n"
            "\n"
            "### Responsibilities\n"
            "\n"
            "| Area | Review focus |\n"
            "| --- | --- |\n"
            "| Booking records | Check organizer, attendee, and event-type relationships |\n"
            "| Availability rules | Keep timezone and date exceptions explicit |\n"
            "\n"
            "### Walkthrough\n"
            "\n"
            "1. Create a booking and confirm its persisted time window.\n"
            "2. Reschedule across a daylight-saving boundary and inspect the stored timestamps.\n"
            "   - Capture the relevant request or job identifier.\n"
            "   - Compare the user-visible outcome with the persisted or provider state.\n"
            "\n"
            "### Failure handling\n"
            "\n"
            "**Watch for:** A migration or slow query can delay the entire booking flow.\n"
            "\n"
            "Suggested diagnostic signals: *connection saturation, lock waits, and booking query latency*. Compare them over the same time window.\n"
            "\n"
            "```text\n"
            "observe the symptom\n"
            "  -> identify the affected dependency\n"
            "  -> reproduce with test data\n"
            "  -> verify recovery from the user perspective\n"
            "```\n"
            "\n"
            "### Readiness checklist\n"
            "\n"
            "- [ ] Exercise the happy path with test data.\n"
            "- [ ] Rehearse the failure and recovery path.\n"
            "- [ ] Record the owner, evidence, and follow-up in the deployment runbook.\n"
            "\n"
            "~~Assume a green process means the workflow works~~ — verify the end-to-end outcome as well.\n"
            "\n"
            "### Frameworks and tools\n"
            "\n"
            "- **Framework layers in this sample**\n"
            "  - No web framework is modeled for this component; inspect its service runtime and integration clients instead.\n"
            "- **Example development and investigation toolkit**\n"
            "  - SQL clients for read-only inspection\n"
            "  - Query plans for index review\n"
            "  - Migration tooling for schema changes\n"
            "- **Example observability tools**\n"
            "  - `prometheus`\n"
            "  - `grafana`\n"
            "  - `loki`\n"
            "  - `jaeger`\n"
            "\n"
            "The tool lists illustrate a possible setup for this architecture; they do not install tools or assert that an upstream project uses every listed tool.\n"
        ),
        version=parse_version("15.0.0"),
        languages=[ProgrammingLanguage.sql],
        deployments=[DeploymentTarget.render],
        owners="Platform",
        metric_tools=[
            MetricTool.prometheus,
            MetricTool.grafana,
            MetricTool.loki,
            MetricTool.jaeger,
        ],
        links=[Link(site_name="Cal.com Docs", http_url=_DOCS)],
    ),
)
redis_block = Manifest(
